	isbn = {978-3-031-36957-5},
	shorttitle = {Do {Emotions} {Matter}?},
	doi = {10.1007/978-3-031-36957-5_32},
	abstract = {Studying emotions in tourism help understand and anticipate tourist behaviour, because emotions can be considered the core of the tourist experience. The measurement of emotions in tourism is a complex research task. Not all negative emotions lead to dissatisfaction and switching to negative behaviour of tourists. Concerning the emotional responses of tourists, it has been found that climate change impacts involve multiple emotional expressions. The purpose of this paper is to identify and analyse the publications of the last eleven years (2012–2022) with respect to the relationships between emotional climate change communication and tourist behaviour. The review results illustrate trends and gaps, and the type of emotions and communication with greater potential to lead behavioural shifts in tourists and tourism stakeholders.},
